title HUNK33 — a named filter is seen before it is committed
prompt Keep taking the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send each increment as its own signed round.
think HUNK32 closed the filter-preset journey (by-name, travels, content-addressed); HUNK13 gave the eye but only for a raw edit-list. The named next crux is the Skate preview of a preset — a keeper sees a filter BY NAME before choosing it, the daily gesture.
think Composed two proven seams: filter_preset.find looks the recipe up by name, edit_preview.preview (pure) previews it as a Skate grid. No new byte-level pipeline, no new failure mode — an unknown name refuses UnknownPreset before a grid, the down-map's own EmptyImage/GridTooLarge surface unchanged.
think Added preview_book — the filter strip — previewing every named filter over one image at once, the property edit_preview alone cannot claim; bounded by max_presets, refuses Overflow on a short slice.
think New file brushstroke/preset_preview.rye; symlinked filter_preset.rye into brushstroke/ (its deps qoi/photo_edits/tally_copy already resolve there), exactly the HUNK13 resolution pattern.
obs Two witness snags, both from re-printing selftest output through sh -c: backticks then an apostrophe (preset's) broke the single-quote wrapping. Dropped both from the GREEN line to match edit_preview's safe pattern.
obs No name stored, no bead written, no funds — a preview is a look, not a commit; the source is read once per named filter and touched never.
loom witness=hunk_preset_preview_witness result=GREEN presets=9 strip_grids=9 lit_pixels=1024 grid=4x4
file brushstroke/preset_preview.rye preview_preset by name + preview_book the filter strip, pure composition over HUNK30 and HUNK13
file brushstroke/filter_preset.rye symlink to image/filter_preset.rye so the preview composes the book's public API
file tools/hunk_preset_preview_witness.rish proves the named preview and the filter strip on metal, refusals named
